# Minecraft Usernames

Never lowercase, uppercase, normalize, or case-fold Minecraft usernames.

Treat names from Bukkit, CoreProtect, tg-bridge registration, and local trust/report tables as exact identifiers. Do not use `toLowerCase(...)`, `toUpperCase(...)`, or `equalsIgnoreCase(...)` for player identity checks.

Use exact matching:

```java
// Bad: different accounts can collapse into the same value.
owner.equalsIgnoreCase(interactorPlayer);
owner.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);

// Good: preserves the actual player identifier.
owner.equals(interactorPlayer);
```

Only transform usernames for display formatting when the transformed value is not used for identity, storage keys, trust checks, report checks, or CoreProtect filtering.
